  "notes": "Duplicate-triage workspace: the session strip pins the tester's crash context (dump, signature, clip) so every result is judged against it. Result cards carry many coded signals: monospace id, colored status pill (green Fixed, blue Open, purple Duplicate, grey Closed), severity in red/orange text, dup count right-aligned, build range 'x → y', platform outline tags, pill-shaped trigger chips (with an orange 'same crash signature' chip), and a colored verdict line ('Reopen candidate', 'Related: link, do not merge', 'Possible duplicate'). Detail pane shows ✓/✗ check chips of overlap with the session, a definition-list grid of report fields, decision option cards with a disabled option explaining why and a SUGGESTED tag, and a prefilled monospace draft with Copy draft primary button. Explicitly labelled 'Rule-based suggestion... Your call.' to avoid AI framing. Keyboard hint '↑ ↓ move between results' and '/' search shortcut. Selected card gets a blue border and slight shadow."
